Description: AI-native multi-track video editor with GPU acceleration
 Palmier Pro for Linux is a multi-track timeline video editor with first-class
 GPU acceleration for NVIDIA, AMD, and Intel graphics and a graceful CPU
 fallback. It is the ground-up C++20 Linux port of Palmier Pro, built with
 Qt 6 (UI), FFmpeg (media/codecs), and Vulkan (GPU compositing and the
 hardware-codec bridge).
 .
 The package bundles the open-source Timeline Editor and the local Model
 Context Protocol (MCP) server, which expose the same editing tool surface to
 the in-app agent chat and to external AI agents over loopback HTTP. These
 components are free software under the GNU GPL v3 (or later) and remain fully
 functional with no network connection to the account-gated generative service.
